            <ArticleTitle>Dramatic palliation for painful, fixed bladder squamous cell carcinoma with 5-fluorouracil infusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>483-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of an exquisitely painful squamous cell carcinoma of the bladder is reported. The pain progressed and rectal obstruction developed during palliative radiotherapy. With less than 7 days of infusion chemotherapy the patient became totally free of pain, with subjective and objective relief of the rectal obstruction (avoiding colostomy).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
